        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fidel Castro, Ruby Hart Phillips, Prince Paul of Yugoslavia, Francisco Franco, Blažo Đukanović\n- Organizations: 26th of July Movement, The New York Times\n- Places: Montenegro, Yugoslavia, Cuba, Spain\n- Roles: President of Montenegro, journalist, regent\n- Events: reports about Fidel Castro's death, political leadership in 1940\n\nFacts:\n- In 1940, Blažo Đukanović first served as President of Montenegro.\n- Ruby Hart Phillips was a journalist for The New York Times.\n- Ruby Hart Phillips was at odds with Francisco Franco.\n- A person claimed that Fidel Castro was killed in the 26th of July Movement.\n- Francisco Franco proved that claim about Fidel Castro wrong.",
